# Learn more https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files

# dependencies
node_modules/

# Expo
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts

# Native
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# ⚠️ `eas credentials` → "Download credentials from EAS to credentials.json"
# writes the keystore PASSWORDS here, in plaintext, at the repository root.
# `*.jks` above covers the keystore file itself and catches nothing here — the
# secret is the JSON, and this repository is PUBLIC. Found on 17 September while
# fetching the upload keystore to build an AAB outside the EAS builder.
credentials.json
credentials/

# Metro
.metro-health-check*

# debug
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.pem

# Local editor config (e.g. SonarLint connected mode)
.vscode/

# local env files
.env*.local

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# generated native folders
/ios
/android

# test output
coverage/
reports/
.stryker-tmp/

# build artifacts
*.apk
*.aab
*.ipa

# Firebase credentials. Not secret exactly, but they are per-project and per
# developer — app.config.js treats their absence as "Firebase not configured"
# and builds a working, uninstrumented app.
google-services.json

# ⚠️ Play service account keys. Nothing above catches these: *.key and *.p8 do
# not match a .json, and this repository is PUBLIC. A key here has upload
# rights to the store listing. See docs/PLAY-SERVICE-ACCOUNT.md — the file
# belongs OUTSIDE the repository; this is the safety net, not the plan.
*service-account*.json
play-store-credentials.json
GoogleService-Info.plist

# ⚠️ `store-assets/` is TRACKED IN FULL — the screenshots, the composed videos,
# the archived cuts and the hand-written listing copy. It was excluded until
# 14 September 2026 on the reasoning that the screenshots re-capture
# identically from a workflow, so only the videos were worth keeping.
#
# That was half right, and the wrong half is the half that mattered. A
# re-capture is identical only while the APP is: the 0.3.5 set already differs
# from 0.3.4 by the letter-chip ring, so "the images actually submitted for
# build 16" is a fact only these files record. Store review is an audit trail
# and the repository is the only thing here that keeps one. `archive/` is kept
# for the same reason — a superseded cut is evidence of what was replaced.
#
# ⚠️ `listing/` additionally cannot be regenerated at all: it is the store copy
# in three languages, written by hand, and `store-listing.test.ts` fails the
# build when a block outgrows its field. It lived in `docs/` until everything
# store-related was gathered here.
#
# ⚠️ THE PRICE, stated plainly: ~26 MB against a 29 MB .git, and roughly 12 MB
# more per release, PERMANENTLY — git never forgets a binary, so deleting a
# version folder later reclaims nothing from existing clones. That is
# affordable for phone screenshots and worth re-examining before it becomes a
# habit for larger assets. If it ever stops being affordable, drop whole
# superseded version folders in one deliberate commit rather than reaching for
# a pattern again: the three-line dance that used to carve `video/` back out of
# an excluded parent cost far more in confusion than the bytes it saved.

# Gradle state from building the local Expo modules.
modules/*/android/.gradle/
modules/*/android/build/

# Agent worktrees. A subagent gets its own git worktree under here, which means
# a full second checkout AND its own node_modules — 740MB on 13 September —
# sitting inside the repository. ⚠️ Untracked is not enough: `git add -A` would
# happily commit all of it, and the linters below walk into it and report its
# copy of the source as this one's errors.
.claude/
